{{!-- The app-wide View switch. One trigger, one item: whichever style you are
     NOT currently on. Same disclosure contract as the modern pill-nav dropdown
     (button + aria-expanded + aria-haspopup over a role="menu" list, driven by
     component state) so it needs no Bootstrap JS and works in both the modern
     navbar and the legacy classic header. --}}
{{#if this.available}}
<div class="ll-viewswitch {{if this.menu_open "is-open"}}">
  <button type="button" class="ll-viewswitch__trigger"
          aria-expanded={{if this.menu_open "true" "false"}}
          aria-haspopup="true"
          aria-label={{t "View style" key="view_style_menu"}}
          {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "toggleMenu")}}>
    <svg class="ll-viewswitch__icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="3"/>
      <line x1="3" y1="9" x2="21" y2="9"/>
      <line x1="9" y1="21" x2="9" y2="9"/>
    </svg>
    <span class="ll-viewswitch__label">{{t "View" key="view_menu_label"}}</span>
    <span class="ll-viewswitch__caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </button>
  {{!-- Two independent axes, deliberately in one menu.

       PRIMARY (Layout: Basic vs Modern) picks the shell and is a different ROUTE on a
       board. SECONDARY (Style: Gentle vs Focused) is an overlay -- a body class -- applied
       on top of whichever layout is active, so all four combinations are reachable.

       Each group lists BOTH of its options rather than only the one you are not on. The
       old single-item form was a toggle wearing a menu's clothes: it never showed which
       state you were in, only where clicking would take you, which reads as a label for
       the CURRENT state to anyone who has not learned otherwise. Listing both with the
       active one checked makes the current state and the alternative visible at once.

       That is why these are `menuitemradio` with `aria-checked` and not plain
       `menuitem`s: the two options in a group are mutually exclusive and exactly one is
       always on, which is what radio semantics mean. The tick is drawn in CSS off
       `.is-selected` and is decoration -- `aria-checked` is what carries the state to a
       screen reader.

       Each option carries a one-line description, because neither axis is self-evident
       from its name alone. The wording is taken from the app's existing copy for the same
       choices (board-actions' board_view_style explainer, and the Gentle/Focused cards in
       components/display-style.js) so the menu cannot drift from the fuller explanations
       those surfaces already give.

       ORDER: each group leads with the option we are steering people to -- Modern, which
       carries the Recommended tag and is where new features land, and Focused, which is
       what a new account is created on (seeded under `new_record?` in
       User#generate_defaults, app/models/user.rb). Putting the badged option first means
       the badge is the first thing read in its group rather than something found after
       the alternative. The order is presentation only: `aria-checked` still reports which
       option is ACTIVE, so leading with the default never implies it is selected.

       The headings are `role="none"` with NO `aria-hidden`. `none` already strips the
       element's own semantics, so adding `aria-hidden` is both redundant and invalid
       (ember-template-lint: no-unsupported-role-attributes) -- and the heading TEXT is
       worth leaving in the accessibility tree, since it is what tells a screen-reader
       user which of the two axes the following item belongs to. --}}
  <ul class="ll-viewswitch__menu" role="menu">
    <li role="none" class="ll-viewswitch__group">{{t "Layout" key="view_group_layout"}}</li>
    <li role="none">
      <button type="button" role="menuitemradio"
              aria-checked={{if this.isClassic "false" "true"}}
              class="ll-viewswitch__item {{unless this.isClassic "is-selected"}}"
              {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "select_view" "modern")}}>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-label">{{t "Modern View" key="card_view"}}<span class="ll-viewswitch__item-tag">{{t "Recommended" key="view_recommended"}}</span></span>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-desc">{{t "Customize your home page and your boards with live-preview tools." key="view_desc_modern"}}</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    <li role="none">
      <button type="button" role="menuitemradio"
              aria-checked={{if this.isClassic "true" "false"}}
              class="ll-viewswitch__item {{if this.isClassic "is-selected"}}"
              {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "select_view" "classic")}}>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-label">{{t "Basic View" key="classic_view"}}</span>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-desc">{{t "A simple side menu, with every tool in one fixed list." key="view_desc_basic"}}</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    <li role="separator" class="ll-viewswitch__sep"></li>
    <li role="none" class="ll-viewswitch__group">{{t "Style" key="view_group_style"}}</li>
    {{!-- "Default" is a statement about NEW accounts, not about this user: Focused is what
         User#generate_defaults seeds under `new_record?`. It reuses the same
         `ll-viewswitch__item-tag` pill as Modern's "Recommended" so the two badges read as
         one system, and stays its own element rather than being baked into the label
         string so it can move or go without touching a translated sentence. --}}
    <li role="none">
      <button type="button" role="menuitemradio"
              aria-checked={{if this.isFocused "true" "false"}}
              class="ll-viewswitch__item {{if this.isFocused "is-selected"}}"
              {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "select_layout" "focused")}}>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-label">{{t "Focused Style" key="view_style_focused"}}<span class="ll-viewswitch__item-tag">{{t "Default" key="view_default"}}</span></span>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-desc">{{t "Stronger contrast and bolder visual cues." key="view_desc_focused"}}</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    <li role="none">
      <button type="button" role="menuitemradio"
              aria-checked={{if this.isFocused "false" "true"}}
              class="ll-viewswitch__item {{unless this.isFocused "is-selected"}}"
              {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "select_layout" "gentle")}}>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-label">{{t "Gentle Style" key="view_style_gentle"}}</span>
        <span class="ll-viewswitch__item-desc">{{t "Softer colors and lighter emphasis." key="view_desc_gentle"}}</span>
      </button>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
{{/if}}
